    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0690" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel Marshall S.
                            Carter to General Marshall
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1947-01-03">3 January 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88932. This afternoon as a matter of coordination I showed Mr. Truman the message
                    I sent you today from Mr. Byrnes.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d362-f1"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0691" n="681" xml:id="pg681"/>
                <p>Mr. Truman suggested that I advise you in the utmost secrecy that he hoped you
                    could be back by 10 January. Mr. Truman’s concern is connected with the last two
                    words of Mr. Byrnes’ message, and the project that the President has previously
                    discussed with you.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
